A rendered object should be selectable for authoring only if it maps to a canonical selector/entity id.\n- Schematic mode is allowed, but it must not imply executable geometry or objective targets unless backed by declared selectors.\n- Literal mode requires provider-declared frame, units, dimensions, geometry/kinematics source, and selector targets.\n- Objective creation should write `StudioObjectiveTermSpec` with explicit source/target selectors. Selecting a generic task/mechanics object is not enough; the authoring flow should resolve to effector position, joint angle, target point, trajectory, or another concrete selector.\n- Task-specific renderers should be registered capabilities or declarative specs, not ad hoc React branches.\n\nAdditional cross-links from prior Scenario Projection work: `5378a5d`, `567405d`, `3c1fc97`, `1b90820`, `0ed9ce3`, `1177849`, `5ec8d0b`, and `bda4721`.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}